{"id":"f6414578bd04e28c5c90bbf881934735291a1c28","url":"https://www.theverge.com/tech/998844/motorola-signature-27-specs-snapdragon-8-elite-extreme-gen-6","title":"Motorola’s wild-looking Signature 27 runs Qualcomm’s new Extreme chipset","site_name":"TechURLs","source":"The Verge","byline":"Dominic Preston","excerpt":"It also features Sony’s latest camera sensor and audio by Bang & Olufsen.","content_html":"<DIV class=\"page\" id=\"readability-page-1\"><div><div><p><a href=\"/authors/dominic-preston\"><img alt=\"Dominic Preston\" data-chromatic=\"ignore\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"36\" height=\"36\" decoding=\"async\" data-nimg=\"1\" srcSet=\"https://platform.theverge.com/wp-content/uploads/sites/2/2025/01/DOM_BLURPLE-1.jpg?quality=90&strip=all&crop=0%2C0%2C100%2C100&w=48 1x, https://platform.theverge.com/wp-content/uploads/sites/2/2025/01/DOM_BLURPLE-1.jpg?quality=90&strip=all&crop=0%2C0%2C100%2C100&w=96 2x\" src=\"https://platform.theverge.com/wp-content/uploads/sites/2/2025/01/DOM_BLURPLE-1.jpg?quality=90&strip=all&crop=0%2C0%2C100%2C100&w=96\"></a></p><div><p><span aria-expanded=\"false\" aria-haspopup=\"true\" role=\"button\" tabindex=\"0\"><span id=\"follow-author-standard_article_details-dmcyOmF1dGhvclByb2ZpbGU6MTI1\"><span><span><svg width=\"9\" height=\"9\" viewBox=\"0 0 9 9\" fill=\"none\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" aria-label=\"Follow\"><path d=\"M5 0H4V4H0V5H4V9H5V5H9V4H5V0Z\" /></svg></span></span><span>Dominic Preston</span></span></span></p> <p><span>is a news editor with over a decade’s experience in journalism. He previously worked at <em>Android Police</em> and <em>Tech Advisor</em>.</span></p></div></div><div id=\"zephr-anchor\"><p>Motorola is the first company to announce a phone running Qualcomm’s top-end <a href=\"/gadgets/998842/qualcomm-snapdragon-8-elite-extreme-gen-6\">Snapdragon 8 Elite Extreme Gen 6 chip</a>. The Signature 27 looks set to be Motorola’s most advanced flagship in some years, though we’re still waiting for the full specs, price, and release date.</p><p>Any prospective buyers will first have to get over the design, which seems guaranteed to earn mixed reception. The aluminum phone has a thin body, available in either black (sorry, “Pantone coal smoke”) or green (“Pantone capulet olive”), with a woven tactical texture on one and a “feather-inspired” finish on the other. Either way, it slopes upwards into what Motorola calls a “camera plane,” with four lenses and a flash in an odd arch layout. It’s certainly unique.</p><p>Only a handful of the Signature 27’s specs have been confirmed, but they’re more appealing to me than the design. The B&amp;O logo by the cameras gives away that Bang &amp; Olufsen has helped design the audio, though the specifics are still unknown. There’s the promise of seven years of Android updates, still rare for Motorola. The cameras will include a 200-megapixel periscope telephoto and a 50-megapixel main camera — the latter is more exciting for using Sony’s LOFIC-enabled Lytia 910 sensor, also seen in this week’s <a href=\"/gadgets/998165/vivo-x500-pro-max-launch-specs-release-date-lofic-china\">Vivo X500 Pro Max</a>, where it enables 17 stops of dynamic range. Hopefully Motorola’s phone matches that.</p><section tabindex=\"-1\" aria-label=\"carousel\"><div id=\":R1obcprar96:\"><p><a href=\"https://platform.theverge.com/wp-content/uploads/sites/2/2026/09/motorola-signature-27-black-chair.jpg?quality=90&strip=all\" data-pswp-height=\"1930\" data-pswp-width=\"2896\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer\"><img alt=\"\" data-chromatic=\"ignore\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" data-nimg=\"fill\" sizes=\"(max-width: 1023px) 100vw, 744px\" srcSet=\"https://platform.theverge.com/wp-content/uploads/sites/2/2026/09/motorola-signature-27-black-chair.jpg?quality=90&strip=all&w=376 376w, https://platform.theverge.com/wp-content/uploads/sites/2/2026/09/motorola-signature-27-black-chair.jpg?quality=90&strip=all&w=384 384w, https://platform.theverge.com/wp-content/upl