gnature 27 are on the way, with a global launch due before the end of the year. Unlike the first Motorola Signature, from earlier this year, that will include the US.</p><div><p><span><strong>Follow topics and authors</strong> from this story to see more like this in your personalized homepage feed and to receive email updates.</span></p><ul><li id=\"follow-author-article_footer-dmcyOmF1dGhvclByb2ZpbGU6MTI1\"><span aria-expanded=\"false\" aria-haspopup=\"true\" role=\"button\" tabindex=\"0\"><span><span><svg width=\"9\" height=\"9\" viewBox=\"0 0 9 9\" fill=\"none\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" aria-label=\"Follow\"><path d=\"M5 0H4V4H0V5H4V9H5V5H9V4H5V0Z\" /></svg></span><span>Dominic Preston</span></span></span></li><li></li><li></li><li></li><li></li><li></li><li></li></ul></div></div></div></DIV>","content_text":"Dominic Preston is a news editor with over a decade’s experience in journalism. He previously worked at Android Police and Tech Advisor.Motorola is the first company to announce a phone running Qualcomm’s top-end Snapdragon 8 Elite Extreme Gen 6 chip. The Signature 27 looks set to be Motorola’s most advanced flagship in some years, though we’re still waiting for the full specs, price, and release date.Any prospective buyers will first have to get over the design, which seems guaranteed to earn mixed reception. The aluminum phone has a thin body, available in either black (sorry, “Pantone coal smoke”) or green (“Pantone capulet olive”), with a woven tactical texture on one and a “feather-inspired” finish on the other. Either way, it slopes upwards into what Motorola calls a “camera plane,” with four lenses and a flash in an odd arch layout. It’s certainly unique.Only a handful of the Signature 27’s specs have been confirmed, but they’re more appealing to me than the design. The B&O logo by the cameras gives away that Bang & Olufsen has helped design the audio, though the specifics are still unknown. There’s the promise of seven years of Android updates, still rare for Motorola. The cameras will include a 200-megapixel periscope telephoto and a 50-megapixel main camera — the latter is more exciting for using Sony’s LOFIC-enabled Lytia 910 sensor, also seen in this week’s Vivo X500 Pro Max, where it enables 17 stops of dynamic range. Hopefully Motorola’s phone matches that.1/6Image: MotorolaMotorola says more details about the Signature 27 are on the way, with a global launch due before the end of the year. Unlike the first Motorola Signature, from earlier this year, that will include the US.Follow topics and authors from this story to see more like this in your personalized homepage feed and to receive email updates.Dominic Preston","fetched_at":"2026-09-24T04:31:21.463Z","ok":true,"blocks":[{"html_en":"<p><span aria-expanded=\"false\" aria-haspopup=\"true\" role=\"button\" tabindex=\"0\"><span id=\"follow-author-standard_article_details-dmcyOmF1dGhvclByb2ZpbGU6MTI1\"><span><span><svg width=\"9\" height=\"9\" viewBox=\"0 0 9 9\" fill=\"none\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" aria-label=\"Follow\"><path d=\"M5 0H4V4H0V5H4V9H5V5H9V4H5V0Z\" /></svg></span></span><span>Dominic Preston</span></span></span></p>","sentences":[{"en":"Dominic Preston","zh":"多米尼克·普雷斯顿"}]},{"html_en":"<p><span>is a news editor with over a decade’s experience in journalism. He previously worked at <em>Android Police</em> and <em>Tech Advisor</em>.</span></p>","sentences":[{"en":"is a news editor with over a decade’s experience in journalism.","zh":null},{"en":"He previously worked at Android Police and Tech Advisor.","zh":null}]},{"html_en":"<p>Motorola is the first company to announce a phone running Qualcomm’s top-end <a href=\"/gadgets/998842/qualcomm-snapdragon-8-elite-extreme-gen-6\">Snapdragon 8 Elite Extreme Gen 6 chip</a>. The Signature 27 looks set to be Motorola’s most advanced flagship in some years, though we’re still waiting for the full specs, price, and release date.</p>","sentences":[{"en":"Motorola is the first company to announce a phone running Qualcomm’s top-end Snapdragon 8 Elite Extreme Gen 6 chip.","zh":null},{"en":"The Signature 27 looks set to be Motorola’s most advanced flagship in some years, though we’re still waiting for the full specs, price, and release date.","zh":null}]},{"html_en":"<p>Any prospective buyers will first have to get over the design, which seems guaranteed to earn mixed reception. The aluminum phone has a thin body, available in either black (sorry, “Pantone coal smoke”) or green (“Pantone capulet olive”), with a woven tactical texture on one and a “feather-inspired” finish on the other. Either way, it slopes upwards into what Motorola calls a “camera plane,” with four lenses and a flash in an odd arch layout. It’s certainly unique.</p>","sentences":[{"en":"Any prospective buyers will first have to get over the design, which seems guaranteed to earn mixed reception.","zh":null},{"en":"The aluminum phone has a thin body, available in either black (sorry, “Pantone coal smoke”) or green (“Pantone capulet olive”), with a woven tactical texture on one and a “feather-inspired” finish on the other.","zh":null},{"en":"Either way, it slopes upwards into what Motorola calls a “camera plane,” with four lenses and a flash in an odd arch layout.","zh":null},{"en":"It’s certainly unique.","zh":null}]},{"html_en":"<p>Only a handful of the Signature 27’s specs have been confirmed, but they’re more appealing to me than the design. The B&amp;O logo by the cameras gives away that Bang &amp; Olufsen has helped design the audio, though the specifics are still unknown. There’s the promise of seven years of Android updates, still rare for Motorola. The cameras will include a 200-megapixel periscope telephoto and a 50-megapixel main camera — the latter is more exciting for using Sony’s LOFIC-enabled Lytia 910 sensor, also seen in this week’s <a href=\"/gadgets/998165/vivo-x500-pro-max-launch-specs-release-date-lofic-china\">Vivo X500 Pro Max</a>, where it enables 17 stops of dynamic range. Hopefully Motorola’s phone matches that.</p>","sentences":[{"en":"Only a handful of the Signature 27’s specs have been confirmed, but they’re more appealing to me than the design.","zh":null},{"en":"The B&O logo by the cameras gives away that Bang & Olufsen has helped design the audio, though the specifics are still unknown.","zh":null},{"en":"There’s the promise of seven years of Android updates, still rare for Motorola.","zh":null},{"en":"The cameras will include a 200-megapixel periscope telephoto and a 50-megapixel main camera — the latter is more exciting for using Sony’s LOFIC-enabled Lytia 910 sensor, also seen in this week’s Vivo X500 Pro Max, where it enables 17 stops of dynamic range.","zh":null},{"en":"Hopefully Motorola’s phone matches that.","zh":null}]},{"html_en":"<p><strong>1<!-- -->/<!-- -->6</strong><span><cite>Image: Motorola</cite></span></p>","sentences":[{"en":"1/6Image: Motorola","zh":null}]},{"html_en":"<p>Motorola says more details about the Signature 27 are on the way, with a global launch due before the end of the year. Unlike the first Motorola Signature, from earlier this year, that will include the US.</p>","sentences":[{"en":"Motorola says more details about the Signature 27 are on the way, with a global launch due before the end of the year.","zh":null},{"en":"Unlike the first Motorola Signature, from earlier this year, that will include the US.","zh":null}]},{"html_en":"<p><span><strong>Follow topics and authors</strong> from this story to see more like this in your personalized homepage feed and to receive email updates.</span></p>","sentences":[{"en":"Follow topics and authors from this story to see more like this in your personalized homepage feed and to receive email updates.","zh":"关注此故事中的主题和作者，以在您的个性化主页源中查看更多类似内容并接收电子邮件更新。"}]},{"html_en":"<li id=\"follow-author-article_footer-dmcyOmF1dGhvclByb2ZpbGU6MTI1\"><span aria-expanded=\"false\" aria-haspopup=\"true\" role=\"button\" tabindex=\"0\"><span><span><svg width=\"9\" height=\"9\" viewBox=\"0 0 9 9\" fill=\"none\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" aria-label=\"Follow\"><path d=\"M5 0H4V4H0V5H4V9H5V5H9V4H5V0Z\" /></svg></span><span>Dominic Preston</span></span></span></li>","sentences":[{"en":"Dominic Preston","zh":"多米尼克·普雷斯顿"}]}],"translated":true,"content_html_zh":"<div class=\"page\" id=\"readability-page-1\"><div><div><p><a href=\"/authors/dominic-preston\"><img alt=\"Dominic Preston\" data-chromatic=\"ignore\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"36\" height=\"36\" decoding=\"async\" data-nimg=\"1\" srcSet=\"https://platform.theverge.com/wp-content/uploads/sites/2/2025/01/DOM_BLURPLE-1.jpg?quality=90&strip=all&crop=0%2C0%2C100%2C100&w=48 1x, https://platform.theverge.com/wp-content/uploads/sites/2/2025/01/DOM_BLURPLE-1.jpg?quality=90&strip=all&crop=0%2C0%2C100%2C100&w=96 2x\" src=\"https://platform.theverge.com/wp-content/uploads/sites/2/2025/01/DOM_BLURPLE-1.jpg?quality=90&strip=all&crop=0%2C0%2C100%2C100&w=96\"></a></p><div><p>多米尼克·普雷斯顿</p> <p>is a news editor with over a decade’s experience in journalism. He previously worked at Android Police and Tech Advisor.</p></div></div><div id=\"zephr-anchor\"><p>Motorola is the first company to announce a phone running Qualcomm’s top-end Snapdragon 8 Elite Extreme Gen 6 chip. The Signature 27 looks set to be Motorola’s most advanced flagship in some years, though we’re still waiting for the full specs, price, and release date.</p><p>Any prospective buyers will first have to get over the design, which seems guaranteed to earn mixed reception. The aluminum phone has a thin body, available in either black (sorry, “Pantone coal smoke”) or green (“Pantone capulet olive”), with a woven tactical texture on one and a “feather-inspired” finish on the other. Either way, it slopes upwards into what Motorola calls a “camera plane,” with four lenses and a flash in an odd arch layout. It’s certainly unique.</p><p>Only a handful of the Signature 27’s specs have been confirmed, but they’re more appealing to me than the design. The B&amp;O logo by the cameras gives away that Bang &amp; Olufsen has helped design the audio, though the specifics are still unknown. There’s the promise of seven years of Android updates, still rare for Motorola. The cameras will include a 200-megapixel periscope telephoto and a 50-megapixel main camera — the latter is more exciting for using Sony’s LOFIC-enabled Lytia 910 sensor, also seen in this week’s Vivo X500 Pro Max, where it enables 17 stops of dynamic range. Hopefully Motorola’s phone matches that.</p><section tabindex=\"-1\" aria-label=\"carousel\"><div id=\":R1obcprar96:\"><p><a href=\"https://platform.theverge.com/wp-content/uploads/sites/2/2026/09/motorola-signature-27-black-chair.jpg?quality=90&strip=all\" data-pswp-height=\"1930\" data-pswp-width=\"2896\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer\"><img alt=\"\" data-chromatic=\"ignore\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" data-nimg=\"fill\" sizes=\"(max-width: 1023px) 100vw, 744px\" srcSet=\"https://platform.theverge.com/wp-content/uploads/sites/2/2026/09/motorola-signature-27-black-chair.jpg?quality=90&strip=all&w=376 376w, https://platform.theverge.com/wp-content/uploads/sites/2/2026/09/motorola-signature-27-black-chair.jpg?quality=90&strip=all&w=384 384w, https://platform.theverge.com/wp-content/uploads/sites/2/2026/09/motorola-signature-27-black-chair.jpg?quality=90&strip=all&w=415 415w, https://platform.theverge.com/wp-content/uploads/sites/2/2026/09/motorola-signature-27-black-chair.jpg?quality=90&strip=all&w=480 480w, https://platform.theverge.com/wp-content/uploads/sites/2/2026/09/motorola-signature-27-black-chair.jpg?quality=90&strip=all&w=540 540w, https://platform.theverge.com/wp-content/uploads/sites/2/2026/09/motorola-signature-27-black-chair.jpg?quality=90&strip=all&w=640 640w, https://platform.theverge.com/wp-content/uploads/sites/2/2026/09/motorola-signature-27-black-chair.jpg?quality=90&strip=all&w=750 750w, https://platform.theverge.com/wp-content/uploads